helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id3160463				0	ru	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Defines graphics export options.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id1				0	ru	When you export graphical elements to a file, you can select the file type. For most supported file types a dialog opens where you can setup export options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id2				0	ru	The following file types do not show an options dialog: PWP, RAS, SVG, TIFF, XPM.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id3				0	ru	The other file types show options dialogs where you can set the width and height of the exported image.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\00\00000200.xhp	0	help	par_id4				0	ru	Depending on the file type, you can specify some more options. Press Shift+F1 and hover over the control to see an extended help text.				20200411 15:09:53
